        "content": "#include <cassert>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <cstdint>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <limits>\n#include <vector>\n\n#if defined(__aarch64__)\n#include <arm_neon.h>\n#endif\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n\n    assert(s < n);\n    assert(n < 8000);\n    assert(s > 0);\n    assert(n > 0);\n\n    const std::size_t width = static_cast<std::size_t>(n);\n    std::vector<int> matrix(width * width);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        const std::size_t row = static_cast<std::size_t>(i) * width;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            std::scanf(\"%d\", &matrix[row + static_cast<std::size_t>(j)]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::vector<std::int64_t> column_sums(width, 0);\n    for (int i = 0; i < s; ++i) {\n        const int* row = matrix.data() + static_cast<std::size_t>(i) * width;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            column_sums[static_cast<std::size_t>(j)] += row[j];\n        }\n    }\n\n    const int window_count = n - s + 1;\n    std::int64_t maximum = std::numeric_limits<std::int64_t>::min();\n\n    for (int top = 0; top < window_count; ++top) {\n        std::int64_t window_sum = 0;\n        for (int j = 0; j < s; ++j) {\n            window_sum += column_sums[static_cast<std::size_t>(j)];\n        }\n        if (window_sum > maximum) {\n            maximum = window_sum;\n        }\n\n        // This scan has a true recurrence: each window starts from its predecessor.\n        for (int j = 1; j < window_count; ++j) {\n            window_sum += column_sums[static_cast<std::size_t>(j + s - 1)] -\n                          column_sums[static_cast<std::size_t>(j - 1)];\n            if (window_sum > maximum) {\n                maximum = window_sum;\n            }\n        }\n\n        if (top + 1 < window_count) {\n            const int* leaving = matrix.data() + static_cast<std::size_t>(top) * width;\n            const int* entering = matrix.data() + static_cast<std::size_t>(top + s) * width;\n            // Columns are independent; widen before subtraction to preserve the full int difference.\n            int j = 0;\n#if defined(__aarch64__)\n            for (; j + 4 <= n; j += 4) {\n                const int32x4_t entering_values = vld1q_s32(entering + j);\n                const int32x4_t leaving_values = vld1q_s32(leaving + j);\n\n                const int64x2_t entering_low = vmovl_s32(vget_low_s32(entering_values));\n                const int64x2_t leaving_low = vmovl_s32(vget_low_s32(leaving_values));\n                const int64x2_t entering_high = vmovl_s32(vget_high_s32(entering_values));\n                const int64x2_t leaving_high = vmovl_s32(vget_high_s32(leaving_values));\n\n                int64x2_t sums_low = vld1q_s64(column_sums.data() + j);\n                int64x2_t sums_high = vld1q_s64(column_sums.data() + j + 2);\n                sums_low = vaddq_s64(sums_low, vsubq_s64(entering_low, leaving_low));\n                sums_high = vaddq_s64(sums_high, vsubq_s64(entering_high, leaving_high));\n                vst1q_s64(column_sums.data() + j, sums_low);\n                vst1q_s64(column_sums.data() + j + 2, sums_high);\n            }\n#endif\n            for (; j < n; ++j) {\n                const std::size_t column = static_cast<std::size_t>(j);\n                column_sums[column] += static_cast<std::int64_t>(entering[j]) - leaving[j];\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", static_cast<long long>(maximum));\n    return 0;\n}\n",
        "path": "src/solution.cpp"
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis": "On the AArch64 target, explicitly updating four independent column sums per NEON iteration may reduce overhead in the O(N²) vertical rolling update. Widening each input before subtraction preserves the full difference between any two valid int values; the dependent horizontal rolling scan remains unchanged.",
